From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] The empty state of Files is text on white

Measured on V90: the middle of an empty folder page is 11.6% grey 239, 5.3%
grey 234 and 3.7% grey 231 -- a fifth of the page, and the last large area of
mid-grey left in the system. Eleven other pages measured in the same round were
92% to 100% white everywhere else.

What draws it is `cabinet.xml`, an 81-line VectorDrawable whose fifteen fills
are all #EFEFEE, #EAEAEA, #CFCFCE, #BDBDBD and one pink #E6A3A3/#E57474. On a
16-level grey panel every one of those lands on level 13, 14 or 15, so the
drawing arrives as a single smudge with no readable shape. `hourglass.xml` is
the same kind of thing. Rule 1 of docs/design/eink-ui.md says those two or three
levels cannot be used to tell one region from another; here they were not even
doing that, they were decoration.

So the three messages this holder shows pass no artwork, the ImageView goes away
when there is none, and the message is centred instead of sitting at the foot of
an otherwise empty screen. The two small dialog icons are untouched: they go to
HeaderMessageDocumentHolder, which is the banner at the top of a listing, not
this full-screen state.

Nothing is removed from the layout and no resource name is added. R.id.artwork
stays, and so does the ImageView, so a message that does want an artwork still
gets one and the resource IDs of this package do not move.

Not run on the device yet when this patch was written.

